export const originals=[[{"title":"Cessna 172L","body":"PROVISIONAL CHECKLIST\n\nMost 172P cards are being used temporarily as placeholders for the 172L while dedicated 172L sections are added. Do not use these procedures operationally until they have been checked against the approved POH/AFM, aircraft placards, equipment, and supplements for the specific airplane.\n\nSelect 172P above to view the original checklist cards."},{"title":"Preflight","body":"Fuel / Oil\nMaster / Flaps / Lights\n\nWALKAROUND\nProp\nOlio\nGear/Brake\nWing\nPitot / Vent / Stall\nAileron (pins/push)\nFlap\nCargo Door\nStab (Elevator/Hinge)\nV Stab (Push/bolts)\nStab (Trim/Elevator/Hinge)\nGear/Brake\nFlap\nAileron (pins/push)\nNose"},{"title":"Before Start","body":"Pax Brief\nSeat/Seatbelts\nParkbrake — Set\n\n?-FLOW\nFuel — Both\nTrim — Set\nMix — In\nThrottle — Cracked\nCarb Heat — In\nAvionics — Off\nBeacon — On\nBreakers — In\nKey — Off\nMaster — Off\nPrime — As Required"},{"title":"Start","body":"Look Out\nMaster — On\nCLEAR\nKey — Start\nRPM — 1,000\nOil Pressure\nAvionics — On"},{"title":"Taxi","body":"Brake Check\nControls — FREE & CORRECT\nInstruments — CHECK IN TURNS"},{"title":"Runup","body":"Primer — LOCKED\nMix — RICH\nClean, Green, 1700\nMags — 125/50\nSuction — CHECK\nVolts — CHECK\nCarb Heat — CHECK\nThrottle — IDLE"},{"title":"Lineup","body":"Traffic\nLights\nCamera (Transponder)\nAction (Flaps)"},{"title":"Takeoff","body":"Flaps — 0\nCarb Heat — COLD\nThrottle — FULL\nLight Wheel\nVR — 60\nVX/VY — 68/85"},{"title":"Downwind / Base / Final","body":"Fuel — Both\nCarb Head — pull\nThrottle\nWhite — Flaps, Trim, Clear\nBase — Clear, Flaps, Trim\nFinal — Clear, Flaps, Trim\nStable — Carb Heat"},{"title":"Electrical malfunctions","body":"AMMETER EXCESSIVE CHARGE\nAlternator — ON; circuit breaker — PULL; nonessential electrical equipment — OFF. Flight — TERMINATE as soon as practical.\n\nLOW-VOLTAGE LIGHT IN FLIGHT\nAvionics power — OFF. Alternator breaker — CHECK IN. Master — OFF (both sides), then ON. Low-voltage light — CHECK OFF. Avionics power — ON.\n\nIf light illuminates again: Alternator — OFF. Nonessential radio/electrical equipment — OFF. Flight — TERMINATE as soon as practical."},{"title":"Engine failures & forced landings (1/2)","body":"ENGINE FAILURE DURING TAKEOFF ROLL\nThrottle IDLE. Brakes APPLY. Flaps RETRACT. Mixture IDLE CUT-OFF. Ignition OFF. Master OFF.\n\nIMMEDIATELY AFTER TAKEOFF\nAirspeed 70 KIAS flaps up / 65 KIAS flaps down. Mixture IDLE CUT-OFF. Fuel selector PUSH DOWN & ROTATE OFF. Ignition OFF. Flaps AS REQUIRED. Master OFF.\n\nDURING FLIGHT — RESTART\nAirspeed 75 KIAS. Carb heat ON. Fuel BOTH. Mixture RICH. Ignition BOTH (START if prop stopped). Primer IN & LOCKED.\n\nEMERGENCY LANDING WITHOUT POWER\nSeats/belts SECURE. Airspeed 70 KIAS flaps up / 65 KIAS flaps down. Mixture IDLE CUT-OFF."},{"title":"Forced landings (2/2) & ditching","body":"EMERGENCY LANDING WITHOUT POWER\nFuel selector OFF. Ignition OFF. Flaps AS REQUIRED (30° recommended). Master OFF. Doors UNLATCH before touchdown. Touchdown SLIGHTLY TAIL LOW. Brakes APPLY HEAVILY.\n\nPRECAUTIONARY LANDING WITH POWER\nSeats/belts SECURE. Flaps 20°. 65 KIAS. Select field; fly over noting terrain, then retract flaps on reaching safe altitude. Electrical switches OFF. Flaps 30° final. 65 KIAS. Master OFF. Doors UNLATCH. Touchdown slightly tail low. Ignition OFF. Brakes heavily.\n\nDITCHING\nTransmit MAYDAY 121.5 with location/intentions. Secure or jettison heavy objects. Belts secure. Approach high winds/heavy seas into wind; light winds/heavy swells parallel to swells. Flaps 20°–30°. Establish 300 ft/min descent at 55 KIAS."},{"title":"Ditching & engine fire on ground","body":"DITCHING\nCabin doors — UNLATCH. Touchdown — LEVEL ATTITUDE at established descent. Face — CUSHION. Evacuate; open window if necessary. Life vests/raft — INFLATE.\n\nFIRE DURING START ON GROUND\nCranking — CONTINUE.\nIf engine starts: Power 1700 RPM for a few minutes; SHUTDOWN and inspect.\nIf engine fails to start: Throttle FULL OPEN. Mixture IDLE CUT-OFF. Cranking CONTINUE. Obtain fire extinguisher. Engine secure: Master OFF, ignition OFF, fuel selector OFF. Extinguish using extinguisher/wool blanket/dirt. Inspect and repair before flight."},{"title":"Engine & electrical fire in flight","body":"ENGINE FIRE IN FLIGHT\nMixture IDLE CUT-OFF. Fuel selector OFF. Master OFF. Cabin heat/air OFF except overhead vents. Airspeed 100 KIAS; increase glide if needed to extinguish. Forced landing — EXECUTE.\n\nELECTRICAL FIRE IN FLIGHT\nMaster OFF. Vents/cabin air/heat CLOSED. Fire extinguisher ACTIVATE. After discharge, ventilate cabin. Avionics power OFF. All other switches except ignition OFF.\n\nIf electrical power is necessary: Master ON. Circuit breakers CHECK for faulty circuit—do not reset. Radio switches OFF. Avionics ON. Electrical switches ON one at a time with delay. Vents OPEN once fire is completely extinguished."},{"title":"Cabin fire, wing fire & icing","body":"CABIN FIRE\nMaster OFF. Vents/cabin air/heat CLOSED. Extinguisher ACTIVATE. Ventilate after discharge. Land as soon as possible.\n\nWING FIRE\nLanding/taxi lights OFF. Pitot heat OFF. Navigation lights OFF. Strobe OFF. Perform sideslip to keep flames away from fuel tank/cabin; land ASAP with flaps retracted if possible.\n\nINADVERTENT ICING\nPitot heat ON. Turn back/change altitude for warmer air. Cabin heat full out; defroster outlets open. Increase power to minimize propeller ice. Continue on next card."},{"title":"Icing, static source & flat tire","body":"INADVERTENT ICING (CONT.)\nWatch for carb ice; apply heat as required. Plan nearest-airport landing; expect higher stall speed. Leave flaps retracted. Open left window and scrape windshield if practical. Forward slip may improve visibility. Approach at 65–75 KIAS depending on ice. Land level attitude.\n\nSTATIC SOURCE BLOCKAGE\nAlternate static source — PULL ON. Airspeed — consult calibration tables.\n\nLANDING WITH A FLAT MAIN TIRE\nApproach NORMAL. Touchdown GOOD TIRE FIRST; hold airplane off flat tire as long as possible."},{"title":"GNS direct-to & route quick reference","body":"DIRECT-TO: press D→, enter/select waypoint, press ENT, then ENT to activate.\n\nWAYPOINT ENTRY\nRotate outer knob to select character position; inner knob to choose character. ENT after last letter. Select latitude/longitude or waypoint memory when required.\n\nCREATE A ROUTE\nFrom NAV/WPT home display choose VIEW/EDIT ROUTE, select route, create/edit waypoints, then activate with START/ENTER.\n\nFLIGHT PLAN\nUse the flight-plan pages to create, edit, delete, or activate routes. Verify every waypoint and course against current charts and ATC clearance."},{"title":"GNS navigation mode notes","body":"To enter Direct-To after selecting a waypoint/route: press D→, confirm identifier, press ENT, then ENT to activate.\n\nNavigation setup notes: select NAV pages with the outer knob; choose desired display with inner knob; confirm sequencing and CDI source before use. Use OBS when suspending automatic waypoint sequencing.\n\nThis legacy handwritten/typed reference is retained as a reminder only—use the installed navigator's approved flight manual supplement."},{"title":"Passenger information","body":"SEAT BELTS\nKeep your seat belt fastened whenever the seat-belt sign is on. When off in flight, keep it loosely fastened while seated.\n\nPORTABLE ELECTRONIC EQUIPMENT\nAM/FM and TV receivers may not be used during flight; these devices may disturb aircraft navigational aids.\n\nFIRE EXTINGUISHERS\nPull tab for removal. Pull pin, aim at base of fire, squeeze handle and sweep.\n\nNo smoking aboard this aircraft. Seat belts must be fastened prior to taxi and takeoff."},{"title":"Emergency exits & extinguisher","body":"EMERGENCY EXITS\nPrimary exits are beside the pilot and forward passenger. To open: pull the door handle up and back to OPEN.\n\nFIRE EXTINGUISHER\nLocated between the pilots' seats. To discharge: remove from holder, pull pin, aim at base of fire and squeeze handle.\n\nCESSNA 172 EMERGENCY INFORMATION\nUse this app as a quick reference only. The approved POH/AFM and current aircraft documents remain controlling."},{"title":"Airspeed limits","body":"LIMIT / MARKING                                      KIAS\n────────────────────────────────────\nVSO — bottom white arc                         40\nVS1 — bottom green arc                         50\nVFE — top white arc                              85\nVNO — top green / bottom yellow       127\nVNE — red line                                     158\nVA @ 2550 lb                                      105\nVA @ 2150 lb                                        95\nVA @ 1750 lb                                        85"}],[{"title":"Skyhawk 1985 Model 172P","body":"PILOT'S CHECKLIST • N99772\n\nA native quick-reference edition rebuilt from the aircraft booklet.\n\nThe pilot's checklist should not be used until the flight crew has become completely familiar with the airplane and systems, all normal and emergency procedure items, and the approved operating limitations.\n\nCessna Aircraft Company • Original issue 20 August 1984"},{"title":"Preflight inspection — overview","body":"Visually check airplane for general condition during walk-around inspection. Use the refueling steps and assist handles if installed; wipe shoes before stepping on upper-wing surfaces. Check for ice, frost, snow, accumulations, and control-surface internal accumulations.\n\nBefore night flight, check all lights and make sure a flashlight is available.\n\nSequence: 1 Cabin • 2 Empennage • 3 Right wing trailing edge • 4 Right wing • 5 Nose • 6 Left wing • 7 Left wing leading edge • 8 Left wing trailing edge"},{"title":"Preflight — cabin, empennage & right trailing edge","body":"CABIN\n1 Pilot's Operating Handbook — AVAILABLE\n2 Parking brake — SET\n3 Control wheel lock — REMOVE\n4 Ignition switch — OFF\n5 Avionics power switch — OFF\n6 Master switch — ON\n7 Fuel quantity indicators — CHECK\n8 Low-vacuum warning light — CHECK ON\n9 Avionics power switch — ON\n10 Avionics cooling fan — CHECK AUDIBLY\n11 Avionics power switch — OFF\n12 Master switch — OFF\n13 Static pressure alternate source — OFF\n14 Fuel selector valve — BOTH\n15 Baggage door — CHECK/LOCK\n\nEMPENNAGE\nRudder gust lock — REMOVE; tie-down — DISCONNECT; controls — CHECK.\n\nRIGHT WING TRAILING EDGE\nAileron — CHECK freedom and security."},{"title":"Preflight — right wing & nose","body":"RIGHT WING\nWing tie-down — DISCONNECT. Main wheel tire — CHECK. Fuel tank sump — DRAIN and check for water/sediment; repeat all drain points until clear. Fuel selector quick-drain — DRAIN. Fuel quantity — CHECK VISUALLY.\n\nNOSE\nEngine oil dipstick/filler — CHECK oil level, secure cap (do not operate with less than five quarts; fill to seven for extended flight). Fuel strainer drain knob — PULL OUT and drain; verify closed. Propeller/spinner — CHECK. Engine cooling air inlets — CLEAR. Carburetor air filter — CHECK. Nosewheel strut/tire — CHECK. Nose tie-down — DISCONNECT. Static source opening — CHECK."},{"title":"Preflight — left wing","body":"LEFT WING\nFuel quantity — CHECK VISUALLY. Fuel filler cap — SECURE. Fuel tank sump quick-drain — DRAIN and check clear. Main wheel tire — CHECK.\n\nLEFT WING LEADING EDGE\nPitot tube cover — REMOVE; opening — CHECK. Fuel tank vent opening — CHECK. Stall warning opening — CHECK (apply suction; horn should sound). Wing tie-down — DISCONNECT. Landing light(s) — CHECK.\n\nLEFT WING TRAILING EDGE\nAileron — CHECK freedom of movement and security."},{"title":"Start & before takeoff (1/2)","body":"BEFORE STARTING ENGINE\nPreflight — COMPLETE. Passenger briefing — COMPLETE. Seats/belts/harnesses — ADJUST & LOCK. Brakes — TEST & SET. Avionics power — OFF. Circuit breakers — CHECK IN. Electrical equipment/autopilot — OFF. Fuel selector — BOTH.\n\nSTARTING ENGINE\nPrime — AS REQUIRED. Carburetor heat — COLD. Throttle — OPEN 1/8 INCH. Mixture — RICH. Propeller area — CLEAR. Master — ON. Ignition — START. Oil pressure — CHECK. Starter — CHECK DISENGAGED. Avionics power — ON. Navigation/flashing beacon — AS REQUIRED. Radios — ON.\n\nBEFORE TAKEOFF\nParking brake — SET. Seats/belts — SECURE. Doors — CLOSED/LOCKED. Controls — FREE & CORRECT. Instruments — CHECK/SET. Fuel — CHECK."},{"title":"Runup — before takeoff (2/2)","body":"Primer — IN & LOCKED. Mixture — RICH. Fuel selector — BOTH. Elevator trim — SET. Throttle — 1700 RPM. Magnetos — CHECK (drop ≤125 RPM each; difference ≤50 RPM). Carb heat — CHECK. Suction gauge — CHECK. Instruments/ammeter — CHECK. Throttle — 1000 RPM or less. Friction lock — ADJUST. Strobes — AS DESIRED. Radios — SET. Autopilot — OFF. Air conditioner — OFF. Wing flaps — SET. Brakes — RELEASE."},{"title":"Takeoff","body":"NORMAL TAKEOFF\nWing flaps — 0°–10°. Carburetor heat — COLD. Throttle — FULL OPEN. Elevator control — LIFT NOSE WHEEL at 55 KIAS. Climb speed — 70–80 KIAS.\n\nSHORT FIELD TAKEOFF\nWing flaps — 10°. Carburetor heat — COLD. Brakes — APPLY. Throttle — FULL OPEN. Mixture — RICH above 3000 feet, LEAN to obtain maximum RPM. Brakes — RELEASE. Elevator control — SLIGHTLY TAIL LOW. Climb speed — 57 KIAS until all obstacles are cleared."},{"title":"Climb, cruise, descent & landing (1/2)","body":"ENROUTE CLIMB\n75–85 KIAS. Throttle FULL OPEN. Mixture RICH above 3000 ft LEAN for max RPM.\n\nCRUISE\nPower 2100–2700 RPM (≤75% recommended). Trim ADJUST. Mixture LEAN.\n\nDESCENT\nFuel selector BOTH. Power AS DESIRED. Mixture ADJUST smooth operation. Carb heat FULL HEAT AS REQUIRED.\n\nBEFORE LANDING\nSeats/belts SECURE. Fuel BOTH. Mixture RICH. Carb heat ON before reducing power. Autopilot OFF. Air conditioner OFF.\n\nNORMAL LANDING\n65–75 KIAS flaps UP. Flaps AS DESIRED (0–10 below 110 KIAS; 10–30 below 85 KIAS)."},{"title":"Landing (2/2) & securing","body":"NORMAL LANDING\n60–70 KIAS flaps DOWN. Touchdown — MAIN WHEELS FIRST. Lower nose gently. Braking — MINIMUM REQUIRED.\n\nSHORT FIELD LANDING\n65–75 KIAS flaps UP; FULL DOWN 30°; 61 KIAS until flare; power REDUCE after obstacle; MAIN WHEELS FIRST; lower nose; flaps UP; BRAKE HEAVILY.\n\nBALKED LANDING\nFULL OPEN. Carb heat COLD. Flaps RETRACT TO 20°. Climb 55 KIAS. Retract flaps after 60 KIAS and obstacle clearance.\n\nAFTER LANDING\nCarb heat COLD. Flaps UP.\n\nSECURING\nParking brake SET. Avionics/electrical/autopilot OFF. Mixture IDLE CUT-OFF. Ignition OFF. Master OFF. Control lock INSTALL."},{"title":"Electrical malfunctions","body":"AMMETER EXCESSIVE CHARGE\nAlternator — ON; circuit breaker — PULL; nonessential electrical equipment — OFF. Flight — TERMINATE as soon as practical.\n\nLOW-VOLTAGE LIGHT IN FLIGHT\nAvionics power — OFF. Alternator breaker — CHECK IN. Master — OFF (both sides), then ON. Low-voltage light — CHECK OFF. Avionics power — ON.\n\nIf light illuminates again: Alternator — OFF. Nonessential radio/electrical equipment — OFF. Flight — TERMINATE as soon as practical."},{"title":"Engine failures & forced landings (1/2)","body":"ENGINE FAILURE DURING TAKEOFF ROLL\nThrottle IDLE. Brakes APPLY. Flaps RETRACT. Mixture IDLE CUT-OFF. Ignition OFF. Master OFF.\n\nIMMEDIATELY AFTER TAKEOFF\nAirspeed 70 KIAS flaps up / 65 KIAS flaps down. Mixture IDLE CUT-OFF. Fuel selector PUSH DOWN & ROTATE OFF. Ignition OFF. Flaps AS REQUIRED. Master OFF.\n\nDURING FLIGHT — RESTART\nAirspeed 75 KIAS. Carb heat ON. Fuel BOTH. Mixture RICH. Ignition BOTH (START if prop stopped). Primer IN & LOCKED.\n\nEMERGENCY LANDING WITHOUT POWER\nSeats/belts SECURE. Airspeed 70 KIAS flaps up / 65 KIAS flaps down. Mixture IDLE CUT-OFF."},{"title":"Forced landings (2/2) & ditching","body":"EMERGENCY LANDING WITHOUT POWER\nFuel selector OFF. Ignition OFF. Flaps AS REQUIRED (30° recommended). Master OFF. Doors UNLATCH before touchdown. Touchdown SLIGHTLY TAIL LOW. Brakes APPLY HEAVILY.\n\nPRECAUTIONARY LANDING WITH POWER\nSeats/belts SECURE. Flaps 20°. 65 KIAS. Select field; fly over noting terrain, then retract flaps on reaching safe altitude. Electrical switches OFF. Flaps 30° final. 65 KIAS. Master OFF. Doors UNLATCH. Touchdown slightly tail low. Ignition OFF. Brakes heavily.\n\nDITCHING\nTransmit MAYDAY 121.5 with location/intentions. Secure or jettison heavy objects. Belts secure. Approach high winds/heavy seas into wind; light winds/heavy swells parallel to swells. Flaps 20°–30°. Establish 300 ft/min descent at 55 KIAS."},{"title":"Ditching & engine fire on ground","body":"DITCHING\nCabin doors — UNLATCH. Touchdown — LEVEL ATTITUDE at established descent. Face — CUSHION. Evacuate; open window if necessary. Life vests/raft — INFLATE.\n\nFIRE DURING START ON GROUND\nCranking — CONTINUE.\nIf engine starts: Power 1700 RPM for a few minutes; SHUTDOWN and inspect.\nIf engine fails to start: Throttle FULL OPEN. Mixture IDLE CUT-OFF. Cranking CONTINUE. Obtain fire extinguisher. Engine secure: Master OFF, ignition OFF, fuel selector OFF. Extinguish using extinguisher/wool blanket/dirt. Inspect and repair before flight."},{"title":"Engine & electrical fire in flight","body":"ENGINE FIRE IN FLIGHT\nMixture IDLE CUT-OFF. Fuel selector OFF. Master OFF. Cabin heat/air OFF except overhead vents. Airspeed 100 KIAS; increase glide if needed to extinguish. Forced landing — EXECUTE.\n\nELECTRICAL FIRE IN FLIGHT\nMaster OFF. Vents/cabin air/heat CLOSED. Fire extinguisher ACTIVATE. After discharge, ventilate cabin. Avionics power OFF. All other switches except ignition OFF.\n\nIf electrical power is necessary: Master ON. Circuit breakers CHECK for faulty circuit—do not reset. Radio switches OFF. Avionics ON. Electrical switches ON one at a time with delay. Vents OPEN once fire is completely extinguished."},{"title":"Cabin fire, wing fire & icing","body":"CABIN FIRE\nMaster OFF. Vents/cabin air/heat CLOSED. Extinguisher ACTIVATE. Ventilate after discharge. Land as soon as possible.\n\nWING FIRE\nLanding/taxi lights OFF. Pitot heat OFF. Navigation lights OFF. Strobe OFF. Perform sideslip to keep flames away from fuel tank/cabin; land ASAP with flaps retracted if possible.\n\nINADVERTENT ICING\nPitot heat ON. Turn back/change altitude for warmer air. Cabin heat full out; defroster outlets open. Increase power to minimize propeller ice. Continue on next card."},{"title":"Icing, static source & flat tire","body":"INADVERTENT ICING (CONT.)\nWatch for carb ice; apply heat as required. Plan nearest-airport landing; expect higher stall speed. Leave flaps retracted. Open left window and scrape windshield if practical. Forward slip may improve visibility. Approach at 65–75 KIAS depending on ice. Land level attitude.\n\nSTATIC SOURCE BLOCKAGE\nAlternate static source — PULL ON. Airspeed — consult calibration tables.\n\nLANDING WITH A FLAT MAIN TIRE\nApproach NORMAL. Touchdown GOOD TIRE FIRST; hold airplane off flat tire as long as possible."},{"title":"GNS direct-to & route quick reference","body":"DIRECT-TO: press D→, enter/select waypoint, press ENT, then ENT to activate.\n\nWAYPOINT ENTRY\nRotate outer knob to select character position; inner knob to choose character. ENT after last letter. Select latitude/longitude or waypoint memory when required.\n\nCREATE A ROUTE\nFrom NAV/WPT home display choose VIEW/EDIT ROUTE, select route, create/edit waypoints, then activate with START/ENTER.\n\nFLIGHT PLAN\nUse the flight-plan pages to create, edit, delete, or activate routes. Verify every waypoint and course against current charts and ATC clearance."},{"title":"GNS navigation mode notes","body":"To enter Direct-To after selecting a waypoint/route: press D→, confirm identifier, press ENT, then ENT to activate.\n\nNavigation setup notes: select NAV pages with the outer knob; choose desired display with inner knob; confirm sequencing and CDI source before use. Use OBS when suspending automatic waypoint sequencing.\n\nThis legacy handwritten/typed reference is retained as a reminder only—use the installed navigator's approved flight manual supplement."},{"title":"Passenger information","body":"SEAT BELTS\nKeep your seat belt fastened whenever the seat-belt sign is on. When off in flight, keep it loosely fastened while seated.\n\nPORTABLE ELECTRONIC EQUIPMENT\nAM/FM and TV receivers may not be used during flight; these devices may disturb aircraft navigational aids.\n\nFIRE EXTINGUISHERS\nPull tab for removal. Pull pin, aim at base of fire, squeeze handle and sweep.\n\nNo smoking aboard this aircraft. Seat belts must be fastened prior to taxi and takeoff."},{"title":"Emergency exits & extinguisher","body":"EMERGENCY EXITS\nPrimary exits are beside the pilot and forward passenger. To open: pull the door handle up and back to OPEN.\n\nFIRE EXTINGUISHER\nLocated between the pilots' seats. To discharge: remove from holder, pull pin, aim at base of fire and squeeze handle.\n\nCESSNA 172 EMERGENCY INFORMATION\nUse this app as a quick reference only. The approved POH/AFM and current aircraft documents remain controlling."},{"title":"Airspeed limits","body":"LIMIT / MARKING                                      KIAS\n────────────────────────────────────\nVSO — bottom white arc                         40\nVS1 — bottom green arc                         50\nVFE — top white arc                              85\nVNO — top green / bottom yellow       127\nVNE — red line                                     158\nVA @ 2550 lb                                      105\nVA @ 2150 lb                                        95\nVA @ 1750 lb                                        85"}]];
